              "id": "b9075279-26d7-34fe-babe-198d81a8ef80",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\n\"Detected Prohibited C Function\" vulnerability in C++ refers to the use of insecure C library functions that can lead to various security issues such as buffer overflows, format string vulnerabilities, or integer overflows. In this case, the function `getenv()` is used, which can lead to security vulnerabilities. The `getenv()` function returns a pointer to a string that is associated with the matched environment variable name. This can lead to potential issues if the environment variable is controlled by an attacker.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nAvoid using `getenv()` function directly. If you need to use environment variables, consider using a secure wrapper function that validates the input and output of the `getenv()` function. \n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\n```cpp\nchar* value;\nconst char* name = \"ROCBLAS_TEST_TIMEOUT\";\nvalue = getenv(name);\nif(value != NULL){\n    // Ensure that the value of the environment variable is safe to use\n    // This is just a simple example, actual validation would depend on how the value is used\n    if(isValid(value)){\n        env = value;\n    }\n}\n```\n\nIn this code, `getenv()` is still used, but the value is validated before being used. The `isValid()` function would need to be implemented to perform appropriate validation for the specific use case.\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe `getenv()` function is part of the C standard library (libc), so no additional libraries are needed for this code.\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP C++](https://owasp.org/www-pdf-archive/OWASP_SCP_v2.pdf)\n- [CWE-676: Use of Potentially Dangerous Function](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/676.html)\n\nPlease note that the links provided are accessible to anonymous users at the time of writing this report."
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "DS154189"
                ]
              }
